.TH P10K\-RS 1 "May 2026" "p10k-rs 0.2.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
p10k\-rs \- Rust port of Powerlevel10k. Single static binary, declarative TOML config, multi-shell prompt.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p10k\-rs
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p10k\-rs
is a from-scratch reimplementation of the Powerlevel10k prompt in Rust.
Configuration is declarative TOML at
.IR ~/.config/p10k\-rs/config.toml ;
the binary renders a prompt per invocation, driven by your shell's
.BR precmd "/" preexec
hooks. Git state on the hot path runs through a long-lived
.BR gitstatusd (1)
daemon (Unix only); macOS, Linux, and Windows all build from the same
codebase.

For interactive setup run
.B p10k\-rs configure
or seed a config from an existing P10K install with
.BR "p10k\-rs import" .

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B prompt
Render a prompt for the given shell. Wired by
.BR precmd / preexec
hooks. Honors
.B \-\-render-side {left|right}
and
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output. The hot path.
.TP
.B init
Print the per-shell init script. Source the output from your shell rc:
.RS
.IP \fBzsh\fR 6
\fBeval "$(p10k\-rs init zsh)"\fR
.IP \fBbash\fR 6
\fBeval "$(p10k\-rs init bash)"\fR
.IP \fBfish\fR 6
\fBp10k\-rs init fish | source\fR
.IP \fBpwsh\fR 6
\fB& p10k\-rs init pwsh | Invoke\-Expression\fR
.RE
.TP
.B configure
Run the interactive configuration wizard. Asks high-level questions
about visual style, segments, and shell integration; writes
.IR ~/.config/p10k\-rs/config.toml .
.TP
.B import
Import a Powerlevel10k
.I ~/.p10k.zsh
file best-effort. Translates the supported subset to TOML; flags
unsupported directives with
.B WARN
on stderr. Idempotent.
.TP
.B statusline
Render a statusline payload for an AI host (Claude Code today; Cursor /
Aider / Goose are stubbed pending upstream protocol). Reads the host's
JSON payload from stdin and writes one styled status line to stdout.
.TP
.B segment\-list
List every segment this build ships, including auto-detect heuristics.
Useful for diagnosing why a segment isn't rendering and for piping into
.BR jq .
.TP
.B config validate
Parse the active TOML config and report any schema errors. Always-on
verification; safe to run from CI.
.TP
.B theme list | show \fIname\fR | install \fIname\fR
Manage bundled prompt themes. List enumerates the catalogue;
.B show
dumps a theme's TOML to stdout; install copies it to the user's config
path (backing up any existing config first).
.TP
.B verify [\-\-binary \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-json]
Verify the
.BR gitstatusd (1)
helper binary against the committed sha256 pin. Exit codes: 0 (match),
2 (mismatch), 3 (binary not found), 4 (host triple not pinned). With
.B \-\-json
emits a single-line object for scripting.
.TP
.B daemon\-health [\-\-json]
Report the per-shell
.BR gitstatusd (1)
daemon's status: alive, wedged, dead, or channel not wired. Exit
codes: 0 (OK), 2 (WEDGED), 3 (DEAD), 4 (NOT_WIRED), 5 (ERROR). With
.B \-\-json
emits a single-line object.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-json]
Run nine runtime probes (Nerd Font, gitstatusd binary, config
present + parses, shell init sourced, instant-prompt cache writable,
OSC 7 support, WSL font story). Exit codes: 0 (all OK / SKIP),
1 (≥1 WARN), 2 (≥1 ERROR). With
.B \-\-json
emits a
.B p10krs.doctor/v1
envelope.
.TP
.B version [\-\-json]
Print binary + bundled-gitstatusd-pin + detected host-triple
diagnostics. Always exits 0. Distinct from
.BR \-\-version ,
which only prints the bare version string.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/p10k\-rs/config.toml
User configuration. See
.B "p10k\-rs configure"
or
.UR https://github.com/scurran1986/powerlevel10k\-rs/blob/main/docs/src/reference/schema.md
the schema reference
.UE .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/p10k\-rs\-$$/
Per-shell daemon FIFO directory. Created by the shell init script and
torn down on shell exit (Unix only).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/p10k\-rs/
Instant-prompt dumps (sanitised
.BR $TERM
in filename, mode 0600). Self-invalidates on terminal switch.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B P10K_RS_CONFIG
Override the resolved config path. Falls through to
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/p10k\-rs/config.toml
and then
.IR ~/.config/p10k\-rs/config.toml .
.TP
.B P10K_RS_GITSTATUSD_BIN
Override the auto-discovered
.BR gitstatusd (1)
binary path.
.TP
.B _P10K_RS_GITSTATUSD_PID_FILE \fR/\fB _P10K_RS_GITSTATUSD_WEDGE
Set by the shell init script when sourced. Their presence is how
.B doctor
and
.B daemon\-health
tell whether your rc is wired.

.SH PLATFORM NOTES
.B Windows
ships a reduced-functionality build: no gitstatusd daemon (FIFO IPC
has no Windows analogue; falls back to
.BR ShellOut ),
no
.B root_indicator
(no EUID), no DECSET 2026 / OSC 4 / TIOCGWINSZ probes (need raw-mode
termios). See the
.B Windows status
page in the mdBook for the per-feature table.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gitstatusd (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1)
